%description:
Tests a route MTU that an ICMP error reports during the path MTU search
(mtuProbing = 2, pmtudEnabled). The scenario is that of tcp_mtu_probe_1, but the
path answers the first probe (B021, MTU 1026) with an ICMP fragmentation-needed
error for an MTU of 1000, and it drops each larger packet. The reported MTU
bounds the search at 1000, as Linux tcp_sync_mss(). The third duplicate ACK,
with the probe as the first unacknowledged segment, then shows the loss: the
search continues from 552 to 1000, and the probe goes again as segments of the
MSS of 600 (B040, B041), without a congestion response. The next probe (736 bytes, MTU 776) stays below the reported MTU, and its ACK raises
the MSS to 736.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 5s
*.srv_app.sendScript="1.0 40000"
*.srv_tcp.mss = 600
*.cli_tcp.mss = 1460
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.srv_tcp.mtuProbing = 2
*.srv_tcp.baseMss = 512
*.srv_tcp.pathMtu = 1500
*.srv_tcp.pmtudEnabled = true
*.tcptester.script="b21 icmp 3 4 mtu 1000"
*.tcptester.pathMtu = 1000

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.017 B020] A.1000 < B.2000: A 11301:11901(600) ack 1 win 16384 
[1.017 B021] A.1000 < B.2000: A 11901:12887(986) ack 1 win 16384 # answering with an ICMP error
[1.017 B022] A.1000 < B.2000: A 12887:13487(600) ack 1 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the route MTU 1000 limits the path MTU search, which runs from 552 to 1000
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the MTU probe of 1026 is lost, the search runs from 552 to 1000
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the lost MTU probe goes again as segments of the MSS, without a congestion response
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.021 B040] A.1000 < B.2000: A 11901:12501(600) ack 1 win 16384 
[1.021 B041] A.1000 < B.2000: A 12501:12887(386) ack 1 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the MTU probe of 776 is acknowledged, snd_mss is 736
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
